\/gameUI\/silicium-high-purity.png?v=1612260629","color":"#cbcdcd","url":"\/en\/items\/detail\/id\/Crystal_Silicon\/name\/Crystal+Silicon"},"Steel":{"className":"Steel","name":"Steel","category":"material","image":"\/img\/gameUI\/steel-plate.png?v=1612260592","description":"Under strict and controllable temperature conditions, using iron ingots as raw material for further smelting, the crystal form of the material is improved so that it has better mechanical properties.","color":"#cbcdcd","url":"\/en\/items\/detail\/id\/Steel\/name\/Steel"},"Plastic":{"className":"Plastic","category":"material","name":"Plastic","description":"Primary chemical product. Has a wide range of uses and is usually used to make more advanced chemical products.","image":"\/img\/gameUI\/plastic.png?v=1612261302","color":"#cbcdcd","url":"\/en\/items\/detail\/id\/Plastic\/name\/Plastic"},"Graphene":{"className":"Graphene","name":"Graphene","category":"material","image":"\/img\/gameUI\/graphene.png?v=1612258252","description":"The double-layer graphenes will form a complex repeating structure, a superlattice by rotating when stack one layer of graphene on top of another.  After rotating to a certain Magic Angle, double-layer graphene will appear superconductivity. Graphene has become a new type of nano-superconducting material.","color":"#cbcdcd","url":"\/en\/items\/detail\/id\/Graphene\/name\/Graphene"},"Carbon_Nanotube":{"className":"Carbon_Nanotube","name":"Carbon Nanotube","category":"material","description":"The weight is very light with a perfectly connected hexagonal structure, has extremely high strength and strong resistance to deformation, and is usually used to manufacture high-efficiency devices.","image":"\/img\/gameUI\/nanotube.png?v=1612258074","color":"#cbcdcd","url":"\/en\/items\/detail\/id\/Carbon_Nanotube\/name\/Carbon+Nanotube"},"Titanium_Ingot":{"className":"Titanium_Ingot","category":"material","name":"Titanium Ingot","description":"Obtained from smelting titanium ores, it 